        "location": "engine/runtime/codex_ownerrules.go:37-49",
        "claim": "rulesFiles does not de-duplicate paths. If CODEX_HOME resolves to the home directory (or the same directory), ~/AGENTS.md and <root>/AGENTS.md are the same file. The block is then written twice, and the message reports it once as written and again as already current. On uninstall the second removal reports nothing. The output is misleading, though the file ends up correct.",
